WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.751
- Fantasy starting five.

00:00:01.751 --> 00:00:04.212
- Whew, it’s a tough decision for the 3:

00:00:04.212 --> 00:00:05.505
KD or Bron.

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:09.175
First thing my teammates said is,
“Man, look at your phone.”

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:12.178
And I looked at it, notifications were
going crazy from the dunk.

00:00:12.721 --> 00:00:16.141
- Shouldn’t a Point God
go first in the NBA draft?

00:00:23.815 --> 00:00:27.861
I'm back on the road, and this time
I'm stopping in Florida to meet Ja Morant.

00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:31.281
This point guard from Murray State has made
a ton of noise in college basketball,

00:00:31.281 --> 00:00:32.741
both on and off the court.

00:00:33.074 --> 00:00:37.495
With the draft approaching he lets us in
on how he’s preparing for the NBA.

00:00:37.495 --> 00:00:40.957
- [Announcer]: Rockin' the cradle
and creating percent

00:00:40.957 --> 00:00:44.627
Too much Ja for Marquette early!

00:00:44.919 --> 00:00:46.713
- All right, Ja Morant,

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:51.259
you went from being barely recruited
to a potential top-three draft pick.

00:00:51.259 --> 00:00:56.222
So when was the moment that you said,
“Hey, I'm, I’m famous now”?

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:57.932
- Um.
- [Laughing]

00:00:57.932 --> 00:01:00.435
- The Alabama game.
We came up short

00:01:00.435 --> 00:01:04.773
but I think I finished with, like,
38 and had a dunk that went viral.

00:01:04.773 --> 00:01:09.194
- [Announcer]: Here, Morant,
12 seconds. Wow!

00:01:09.194 --> 00:01:12.864
- I was gettin’ on the bus after the game.
First thing my teammates said is,

00:01:12.864 --> 00:01:14.115
“Man, look at your phone.”

00:01:14.115 --> 00:01:17.202
And I looked at it, notifications
were going crazy from the dunk.

00:01:17.202 --> 00:01:19.913
- [Announcer]: 36 points, he’s showin’ off tonight.

00:01:19.913 --> 00:01:22.791
- Now I know after your
NCAA tournament win,

00:01:22.791 --> 00:01:26.169
you gained about 100,000 followers
on Instagram, right?

00:01:26.169 --> 00:01:27.587
- Yeah.
- How did that feel?

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:33.134
- It felt good, but honestly, I think the win,
first time gettin’ a win—you know, it felt great.

00:01:33.134 --> 00:01:35.929
- But of those follows, which were the coolest?

00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:44.521
- I’d probably have to say the players in the NBA:
Kevin Durant, Luka, Paul George.

00:01:44.521 --> 00:01:47.440
One that probably stand out
right now is Allen Iverson.

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:53.113
Somebody that I kinda grew up watching,
looking at, he followed me and DMed me.

00:01:53.488 --> 00:01:55.031
- Allen Iverson DMed you?

00:01:55.031 --> 00:01:56.407
- Yeah.
- What'd he say?

00:01:56.407 --> 00:01:58.660
- He was just like,
“Just keep working”

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:00.995
and basically telling me
that I was very talented.

00:02:00.995 --> 00:02:02.997
- Well, I have another message for you.

00:02:02.997 --> 00:02:06.793
I told CJ McCollum that I was
going to be interviewing you,

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:08.920
and he sent a video for me to show you.

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:09.671
Ready?

00:02:09.671 --> 00:02:14.634
- What up, Taylor? I heard you got one of them
mid-major killers coming in town this week.

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:17.262
Ja, I wish you nothing but the best
at the next level.

00:02:17.262 --> 00:02:21.724
Understand that you have a responsibility
coming from a mid-major program, man.

00:02:21.724 --> 00:02:25.854
Be a monster. Be a killer.
Be a savage. Don't lose your chip.

00:02:25.854 --> 00:02:29.732
You know, how you play will affect the next Ja.
It will affect the next CJ.

00:02:29.732 --> 00:02:32.944
It will affect the next Dame, the next Steph.

00:02:32.944 --> 00:02:34.737
So keep that pipeline open.

00:02:34.737 --> 00:02:37.824
Wish you nothing but success,
except for when you play against us.

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:44.205
- But, so, he talks about just this responsibility
that you now have, making it from a mid-major.

00:02:44.205 --> 00:02:46.207
Is that how you feel, that the way that you play

00:02:46.207 --> 00:02:50.837
is going to be the way we perceive
mid-major players coming forward?

00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:53.006
- Yeah, I think those guys—

00:02:53.006 --> 00:02:54.382
CJ, Dame and Steph—

00:02:54.382 --> 00:02:57.385
kinda open it up for
some other mid-major players,

00:02:57.385 --> 00:02:59.888
and most of them probably
have the same story.

00:02:59.888 --> 00:03:02.891
Falling under the radar
and end up blowing up late,

00:03:02.891 --> 00:03:05.226
and now everybody's like, “Who is this guy?”

00:03:05.226 --> 00:03:09.189
And all three of those guys
now is big-time players in the NBA,

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:12.775
and hopefully when I get there,
I can be one of those players.

00:03:14.861 --> 00:03:19.032
- With the draft coming up,
lots of decisions to be made with your suit.

00:03:19.032 --> 00:03:22.660
What kind of statement do you want to
make with what you wear on draft night?

00:03:23.119 --> 00:03:28.374
- I'm a fashion guy. I like dressing.
I love shoes. So I'mma be different.

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:31.711
- OK, since you're a fashion guy,
I’mma show you some suits.

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:33.838
You give me your thoughts, you grade the suit.

00:03:33.838 --> 00:03:35.215
LeBron.

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:40.678
- Come on, Bron.
I don't know what color that is, honestly.

00:03:40.678 --> 00:03:44.933
Then the fit is just, like—
my wrist probably can fit in there too.

00:03:44.933 --> 00:03:46.851
That's gotta go with a C.

00:03:46.851 --> 00:03:48.144
- Only a C?

00:03:48.144 --> 00:03:49.103
- Yeah, cuz it’s Bron.

00:03:49.103 --> 00:03:50.230
- Damian Lillard.

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:52.523
- I just like how he throw it off a little bit,

00:03:52.523 --> 00:03:55.526
have the different colors,
but it all in sync together.

00:03:55.526 --> 00:03:57.153
That's an A to me right there.

00:03:57.153 --> 00:03:58.238
- All right, Steph.

00:03:59.822 --> 00:04:00.823
- Ahhh.

00:04:00.823 --> 00:04:01.991
- That's a yikes.

00:04:01.991 --> 00:04:03.701
- Yeah, I don't know about the color.

00:04:03.701 --> 00:04:07.413
The fit a little big too,
cuz I know his legs not that big.

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:11.626
But again, it's Steph, so he get a C.

00:04:11.626 --> 00:04:12.418
- He gets a C?

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:12.961
- Yeah.

00:04:12.961 --> 00:04:13.836
- Trae Young.

00:04:15.255 --> 00:04:18.091
- It's different.
I think he should have pulled it up a little bit.

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:20.009
Like, it look like capris almost.

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:22.053
He get a C-plus.

00:04:22.637 --> 00:04:25.390
- And what do you think of the
“They will know your name” in the jacket?

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:28.268
- That’s tough.
It’s basically like he tryin’ to prove himself.

00:04:28.268 --> 00:04:30.520
- If there was a message
that you could put in a suit,

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:31.896
what would your message be?

00:04:31.896 --> 00:04:34.524
- “Beneath no one.”
That's what my mom always told me.

00:04:34.524 --> 00:04:36.985
I probably would have to add “Trained to go” too.

00:04:36.985 --> 00:04:39.279
That, like, basically I was built for this moment.

00:04:39.279 --> 00:04:41.447
- So, “Beneath no one” and “Trained to go.”

00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:42.156
- Yeah.

00:04:42.156 --> 00:04:42.448
- I like it.

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:48.162
- Seat belts!

00:04:49.372 --> 00:04:50.999
Oh, this is actually smooth.

00:04:50.999 --> 00:04:54.085
- Yeah, I noticed. This a little faster too.

00:04:55.753 --> 00:04:59.173
- You're working out at this world-class facility.

00:04:59.173 --> 00:05:00.174
- Yeah.

00:05:00.174 --> 00:05:04.178
- In a couple weeks, you’ll be an NBA player.

00:05:05.471 --> 00:05:08.016
Like, I feel like you're just, like, “Yeah, cool.”

00:05:08.016 --> 00:05:10.143
- Nah, this right here is, is crazy.

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:13.104
IMG, me being able to work out here

00:05:13.104 --> 00:05:16.065
with all the stuff they have,
I’ve almost been to the NBA's.

00:05:19.485 --> 00:05:22.739
- So what's your goal while you're
training here at the IMG Academy?

00:05:22.739 --> 00:05:25.533
- I’d say the biggest is probably getting stronger.

00:05:26.451 --> 00:05:30.955
The physicality in the NBA is different
than college, and also probably conditioning.

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:35.793
Obviously, I'll probably be playing
50-plus more games than I did in college.

00:05:35.793 --> 00:05:39.088
Just to be in the best shape
I can be for those 82 games.

00:05:41.674 --> 00:05:43.634
- You also do some yoga here.

00:05:43.634 --> 00:05:44.093
- Yeah.

00:05:44.093 --> 00:05:46.679
- Have you benefited from the zen of yoga?

00:05:46.679 --> 00:05:48.639
- Yeah, my body was a little tight.

00:05:49.057 --> 00:05:51.225
And we actually did yoga a little bit

00:05:51.225 --> 00:05:54.103
before the season at Murray,
and I was struggling.

00:05:54.103 --> 00:05:57.899
And since I've been here,
I've been doing yoga once a week,

00:05:57.899 --> 00:06:01.652
and I feel like my body is
getting better and more flexible.

00:06:01.652 --> 00:06:03.279
- What's the best pose that you do?

00:06:03.696 --> 00:06:06.574
- Just laying down.
The end, when you gotta relax and go to sleep.

00:06:06.866 --> 00:06:08.451
- [Laughing] That’s where you excel?

00:06:08.618 --> 00:06:10.203
- Yeah, everything else hurt.

00:06:13.373 --> 00:06:16.209
- I know you said you haven't golfed yet,
but you said you wanted to golf.

00:06:16.209 --> 00:06:18.586
Why golf? And are you gonna be bad?

00:06:18.878 --> 00:06:22.548
- Um, I'm pretty sure I will be bad.

00:06:25.968 --> 00:06:28.262
- You were so confident too! I was ready.

00:06:28.262 --> 00:06:30.890
I know, it just went so far we can't see it.

00:06:34.435 --> 00:06:35.895
- OK. No, do your, do your—

00:06:35.895 --> 00:06:36.854
- You messed me up!

00:06:36.854 --> 00:06:37.522
- No, do, do your—

00:06:37.522 --> 00:06:38.106
- You messed me up!

00:06:38.106 --> 00:06:38.815
- [Laughing]

00:06:38.815 --> 00:06:39.649
- You messed me up.

00:06:39.649 --> 00:06:40.608
- I'm helping you out.

00:06:40.608 --> 00:06:45.488
- Right! Cuz I was a PGA champ
before you stepped in!

00:06:47.448 --> 00:06:48.032
- Ohhh.

00:06:48.032 --> 00:06:50.576
- Nice, Taylor, nice.

00:06:51.411 --> 00:06:55.790
- All right, Ja. Boom!
I missed a couple shots, but I hit the golf ball.

00:06:57.083 --> 00:06:58.084
- All right.

00:06:58.084 --> 00:06:59.544
- You athletic, you should be able to hit the ball.

00:06:59.544 --> 00:07:01.295
- You got it. You got it this time.

00:07:01.295 --> 00:07:04.132
- Don't worry about it.
I’m ‘bout to knock it out the park.

00:07:08.678 --> 00:07:09.345
Man, what?!

00:07:09.345 --> 00:07:10.680
- That was good though.

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:12.348
- Look where my ball at, man.

00:07:12.348 --> 00:07:13.141
- Baby steps.

00:07:14.767 --> 00:07:21.441
- [Announcer]: The tournament’s two leading
scorers, up, hammers it home! It’s a Ja jam!

00:07:21.774 --> 00:07:26.654
- It's just crazy to me that you were able to
really slip through the cracks of every school.

00:07:26.654 --> 00:07:27.697
How does that happen?

00:07:28.614 --> 00:07:32.368
- A question I asked myself
around those times. It was rough.

00:07:32.368 --> 00:07:34.745
There was times where I was
thinking about just quitting.

00:07:35.037 --> 00:07:37.248
It was like, “What do I gotta do?”

00:07:37.248 --> 00:07:41.294
Like, I felt like I proved myself
against some of the top teams,

00:07:41.294 --> 00:07:44.714
top players, and still nobody offered me.

00:07:45.506 --> 00:07:47.842
- And how did you convince
yourself to keep going?

00:07:47.842 --> 00:07:49.469
- I think it was more of my parents.

00:07:49.635 --> 00:07:52.555
I mean, once you get down and
start questioning yourself,

00:07:52.555 --> 00:07:56.684
it's hard to get back, and my parents
just told me to just keep working.

00:07:57.018 --> 00:07:58.478
It ended up paying off, so.

00:07:58.478 --> 00:08:00.897
- But if you could just tell your parents something

00:08:00.897 --> 00:08:03.649
about helping you with your journey,
what would it be?

00:08:03.649 --> 00:08:06.694
- I love them.
I don’t think I can thank them enough.

00:08:06.694 --> 00:08:08.529
The negative things my dad would say,

00:08:08.529 --> 00:08:11.824
my mom yelling at him for
the negative things he’d say.

00:08:11.824 --> 00:08:14.702
- How did that tough love
from your dad help you?

00:08:14.702 --> 00:08:19.332
- He probably would call me overrated,
say I haven't done anything yet.

00:08:19.332 --> 00:08:22.210
I think I finally understood,
like, what he was doing cuz

00:08:22.210 --> 00:08:24.962
he really prepared me for
what was gonna happen.

00:08:24.962 --> 00:08:28.633
Like, mainly a lot this year.
Obviously my name blew up,

00:08:28.633 --> 00:08:32.720
so every away game,
if the fans yellin’ “overrated”—

00:08:32.720 --> 00:08:34.764
- “I heard that. My dad told me that.”

00:08:34.764 --> 00:08:36.807
- Yeah, like, it doesn't bother me.

00:08:36.807 --> 00:08:39.519
If I can take it from my dad,
I can take it from anybody.

00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:51.948
- Game’s still not over cuz you hit it.
Game’s still on the line.

00:08:52.615 --> 00:08:54.825
Let me see your form before you hit it.

00:08:54.825 --> 00:08:55.701
- I don’t even know—

00:08:55.701 --> 00:08:56.702
- I know, cuz I'm like—

00:08:56.702 --> 00:08:58.913
- I still don't feel like I'm holding the thing right.

00:08:58.913 --> 00:09:00.414
- I’mma move, actually.

00:09:01.791 --> 00:09:02.750
- You got this.

00:09:03.793 --> 00:09:04.794
- Go, Ja!

00:09:06.462 --> 00:09:09.465
- [Laughing]

00:09:09.465 --> 00:09:11.968
- So I'mma let you play some
fantasy basketball right now.

00:09:11.968 --> 00:09:14.762
If you could pick any players in the league—

00:09:14.762 --> 00:09:17.557
current players, including yourself—
who's on your team?

00:09:17.557 --> 00:09:20.226
- Well, I have to go with me first,
point guard.

00:09:20.768 --> 00:09:23.729
I like Paul George to be my 2.
He also plays defense.

00:09:24.188 --> 00:09:28.693
Whew, it’s a tough decision for the 3.
I don't know if I'd pick KD or Bron.

00:09:29.235 --> 00:09:32.363
Probably KD because Bron, he can make plays,

00:09:32.363 --> 00:09:35.324
but I feel like I can be that facilitator for this team.

00:09:36.617 --> 00:09:40.663
For the 4, I’mma have to go with Greek Freak.

00:09:41.205 --> 00:09:42.707
- OK, this is a squad. OK.

00:09:43.124 --> 00:09:47.295
- For my 5, AD.
Anthony Davis.

00:09:47.587 --> 00:09:48.254
- That's good.

00:09:48.254 --> 00:09:48.796
- Yeah.

00:09:49.589 --> 00:09:52.842
- Who are you gonna enjoy throwing
lobs to the most on that team?

00:09:54.510 --> 00:09:57.763
- Man, probably Anthony Davis.

00:09:58.848 --> 00:10:02.310
Probably be that pick-and-roll,
and you can just throw it anywhere

00:10:02.310 --> 00:10:03.769
around the rim, he’ll just go get it.

00:10:05.104 --> 00:10:07.815
- I was watching an interview
when you referenced Drake's lyric.

00:10:07.815 --> 00:10:10.610
Like, that's around the time that
your idols become your rivals.

00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:11.027
- Yeah.

00:10:11.027 --> 00:10:12.445
- How does that line relate to you?

00:10:13.154 --> 00:10:14.488
- It's gonna relate
a lot soon.

00:10:14.488 --> 00:10:19.910
Once I get in the NBA,
watching guys that I grew up watching,

00:10:19.910 --> 00:10:22.330
honestly, who've been there
in the NBA for a while

00:10:22.330 --> 00:10:24.290
and stepping on the same court as them.

00:10:24.290 --> 00:10:28.044
It’s gonna feel great, but at the same time,

00:10:28.044 --> 00:10:29.462
you can’t have no friends on the court.

00:10:29.462 --> 00:10:32.089
- Which basketball player,
though, is it gonna be, like,

00:10:32.089 --> 00:10:35.426
it'll take you a minute to say,
“All right, this is my opponent.

00:10:35.426 --> 00:10:38.512
I can't, like, appreciate them as
a basketball player right now”?

00:10:38.512 --> 00:10:39.555
Who's that one player?

00:10:39.680 --> 00:10:40.640
- Westbrook.

00:10:40.931 --> 00:10:41.265
- Yeah.

00:10:41.766 --> 00:10:44.644
- My favorite player. I got a lot of love for him.

00:10:44.644 --> 00:10:50.483
And once I step in those four lines again
against him, it's just gonna be a battle.

00:10:50.483 --> 00:10:53.110
- So what have you taken from his game?

00:10:53.110 --> 00:10:54.779
- I just like what he do on the floor.

00:10:54.779 --> 00:10:57.073
He try to do everything he
can to help his team win.

00:10:57.073 --> 00:11:00.409
If it's rebounding the ball,
making plays for his teammate

00:11:00.409 --> 00:11:03.871
or score the ball,
and that's kinda how I try to play.

00:11:03.871 --> 00:11:05.873
Just do anything I can to help my team win

00:11:05.873 --> 00:11:07.458
and just try to play an all-around game.

00:11:10.211 --> 00:11:14.090
- For every guest that I have on the show,
we do a “Take Me” segment,

00:11:14.090 --> 00:11:16.092
and that's what we're gonna
do right now, OK?

00:11:16.092 --> 00:11:20.054
Take me to your first win in basketball.

00:11:20.054 --> 00:11:22.765
- My first year in AAU
when I played with my dad.

00:11:22.765 --> 00:11:25.851
I think the most thing I remember about
it is when our coaches,

00:11:25.851 --> 00:11:28.646
like, telling us to keep our hands out
when we play defense.

00:11:28.646 --> 00:11:31.023
So he started this little chant
called Airplane.

00:11:31.023 --> 00:11:33.943
So, like, we would be playing defense
and everybody be screaming it.

00:11:33.943 --> 00:11:35.736
- “Airplane.”
- Yeah.

00:11:35.736 --> 00:11:39.281
- Take me to the inspiration
for the eyebrow cuts.

00:11:40.991 --> 00:11:44.370
- Well, my dad had ‘em when he was in school.
- OK.

00:11:44.370 --> 00:11:46.914
- It did look a little, I guess, cool

00:11:46.914 --> 00:11:51.001
and you probably don't see
most people with ‘em.

00:11:51.001 --> 00:11:52.378
I got the same ones.

00:11:52.378 --> 00:11:54.547
- Do you do ‘em on your own or
do you go to the barber and he does it for you?

00:11:54.547 --> 00:11:57.007
- He actually—my dad’s a barber.
- Nice.

00:11:57.007 --> 00:11:59.927
- So he cuts my hair and do the
things in my eyebrows and all.

00:12:00.845 --> 00:12:04.056
- All right, take me to playing
AAU with Zion Williamson.

00:12:04.056 --> 00:12:09.061
- We won a lot of games.
It wasn’t too many losses we had.

00:12:09.186 --> 00:12:13.774
- So when you guys were playing,
did you know the path Zion was going to take?

00:12:13.774 --> 00:12:15.860
- I knew he would be a special talent.

00:12:15.860 --> 00:12:18.612
He was a rising freshman. I was in 10th grade.

00:12:18.612 --> 00:12:23.743
He was playing up with us and
was scoring easy against older guys,

00:12:23.743 --> 00:12:25.244
so I always knew he had it in him.

00:12:27.371 --> 00:12:33.377
- You have called yourself “The Point God.”
Shouldn’t a Point God go first in the NBA draft?

00:12:37.840 --> 00:12:38.674
- Oh, man.

00:12:38.674 --> 00:12:41.802
Well, most people,
they blowin’ up the Point God thing,

00:12:41.802 --> 00:12:46.390
saying I’m arrogant and cocky,
but what they don’t know is

00:12:46.390 --> 00:12:49.143
me and my dad been sayin’
it since I was playing.

00:12:49.143 --> 00:12:53.522
And that’s just me being humble
and confident at the same time.

00:12:53.522 --> 00:12:59.779
I feel like I am a top player in this draft,
but regardless of where I go—

00:12:59.779 --> 00:13:04.825
first, second, third—I’mma still be the same Ja

00:13:04.825 --> 00:13:07.328
and just try to make an impact
on whatever team draft me.

00:13:08.319 --> 00:13:10.623
[Announcer:] Step back Ja again

00:13:10.623 --> 00:13:15.294
He told us all, "Relax. I'm not done yet.

00:13:15.544 --> 00:13:17.811
- Ja Morant on the show today,
which, by the way:

00:13:17.825 --> 00:13:21.996
We call you Ja, but your real name is—
- Temetrius.

00:13:22.122 --> 00:13:23.916
- And your middle name is—
- Jamel.

00:13:23.916 --> 00:13:25.334
- And that’s where we get Ja.

00:13:25.445 --> 00:13:27.351
- Yeah. Honored to be on.

00:13:27.351 --> 00:13:29.767
- Oh, we’re happy to have you on.
Thank you.

00:13:33.319 --> 00:13:34.487
- Man, I quit!

00:13:34.738 --> 00:13:37.441
- You can’t quit!
Remember, we don’t quit around here.

